.TH CHTTPSVR_DECLARE_SCOPED 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_declare_scoped \- declare a chttpsvr variable with automatic destruction
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

chttpsvr_declare_scoped(name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Like chttpsvr_declare, but the variable also carries a GCC cleanup
attribute.  When name goes out of scope the server is destroyed in
the same way as chttpsvr_destroy destroys it.  The macro sets the
variable to CHTTPSVR_NULL, and if name still holds that value at
the end of the scope the cleanup does nothing.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_construct_scoped (3),
.BR chttpsvr_declare (3)
